'''''UFC Fight Night: Procházka vs. Stirling''''' (also known as '''''UFC Fight Night 294''''') is an upcoming [[mixed martial arts]] event produced by the [[Ultimate Fighting Championship]] that is scheduled to take place on November 21, 2026, at the [[Ali Bin Hamad al-Attiyah Arena]] in [[Al Rayyan (city)|Al Rayyan]], Qatar.<ref name="qatar">{{Cite web|url=https://mmajunkie.usatoday.com/story/sports/ufc/2026/09/17/ufc-fight-night-qatar-november/91806430007/|title=UFC announces return to Qatar with Fight Night event this fall|publisher=mmajunkie.usatoday.com|author=Farah Hannoun|date=2026-09-17|access-date=2026-09-18}}</ref>

==Background==
The event will mark the promotion's second visit to Qatar and first since [[UFC Fight Night: Tsarukyan vs. Hooker]] in November 2025.<ref name="qatar"/>

A light heavyweight bout between former [[UFC Light Heavyweight Championship|UFC Light Heavyweight Champion]] (also the inaugural [[Rizin Fighting Federation#Light Heavyweight Championship|Rizin Light Heavyweight Champion]]) [[Jiří Procházka]] and [[Navajo Stirling]] is scheduled to headline the event.<ref name="main">{{Cite web|url=https://www.mmafighting.com/ufc/513140/jiri-prochazka-vs-navajo-stirling-8-other-fights-official-for-ufc-qatar|title=Jiri Prochazka vs. Navajo Stirling, 8 other fights official for UFC Qatar|publisher=mmafighting.com|author=Guilherme Cruz|date=2026-09-29|access-date=2026-09-29}}</ref>

A lightweight bout between [[Magomed Zaynukov]] and Manoel Sousa was reportedly scheduled for the event.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.si.com/fannation/mma/news/ufc-qatar-reportedly-adds-huge-fight-featuring-undefeated-islam-makhachev-teammate|title=UFC Qatar reportedly adds huge fight featuring undefeated Islam Makhachev teammate|publisher=si.com|author=Drew Beaupre|date=2026-09-26|access-date=2026-09-27}}</ref> However, Zaynukov stated he had not signed a contract for the fight and would not compete again in 2026 due to an operation, leaving it unclear whether a replacement opponent would be found for Sousa.<ref name="Sousa">{{Cite web|url=https://www.sportscapemagazine.com/blog/magomed-zaynukov-withdraws-from-reported-ufc-qatar-fight-with-manoel-sousa-due-to-physical-issues|title=Magomed Zaynukov withdraws from reported UFC Qatar fight with Manoel Sousa due to physical issues|publisher=sportscapemagazine.com|author=Rohit Gupta|date=2026-09-28|access-date=2026-09-28}}</ref>

A welterweight bout between [[Jake Matthews (fighter)|Jake Matthews]] and promotional newcomer [[Akbar Abdullaev]] was initially announced for this event.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.fightmag.com/ufc-qatar-main-event-jiri-prochazka-faces-navajo-stirling/|title=UFC Qatar main event: Jiri Prochazka faces Navajo Stirling|publisher=fightmag.com|author=Parviz Iskenderov|date=2026-09-29|access-date=2026-09-30}}</ref> However, Abdullaev will not compete at the event due to the promotion making a mistake with the matchup. As a result, Matthews will meet Tahir Abdullayev instead.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://bloodyelbow.com/2026/09/29/ufc-makes-mistake-with-ufc-qatar-announcement-as-undefeated-dwcs-star-is-taken-off-event/|title=UFC makes mistake with UFC Qatar announcement as undefeated DWCS star is taken off event|publisher=bloodyelbow.com|author=Jamie Theodosi|date=2026-09-29|access-date=2026-09-30}}</ref>

Former [[Legacy Fighting Alliance#LFA Women's Bantamweight Championship|LFA Women's Bantamweight Champion]] [[Jacqueline Cavalcanti]] and Michelle Montague were expected to meet in a women's bantamweight bout.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://agfight.com/ufc/jacqueline-cavalcanti-enfrenta-carrasca-brasileira-no-ufc-catar-em-novembro/|title=Jacqueline Cavalcanti enfrenta carrasca brasileira no UFC Catar, em novembro|publisher=agfight.com|author=Neri Fung|date=2026-10-07|access-date=2026-10-07}} {{in lang|pt-br}}</ref> However, the pairing was postponed to [[UFC 335]] three weeks later for undisclosed reasons.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/report-jacqueline-cavalcanti-vs-michelle-000108379.html|title=Report: Jacqueline Cavalcanti vs. Michelle Montague postponed to UFC 335 on Dec. 12|publisher=sports.yahoo.com|author=Sayan Nag|date=2026-11-01|access-date=2026-11-02}}</ref>

